Version 4.1
SHEET 1 1244 1176
WIRE 80 128 80 112
WIRE 112 128 112 112
WIRE -64 144 -80 144
WIRE -16 144 -32 144
WIRE 48 144 16 144
WIRE 64 144 48 144
WIRE 208 144 192 144
WIRE -112 176 -112 160
FLAG -112 176 0
FLAG 208 144 0
FLAG 48 144 in
SYMBOL Sources\\v_1phase_2 -112 144 R0
SYMATTR Value U1Nenn={100*hz50}  frequ={fn1} Texp=0m tpwl=40m TD=0 fact=0.8165 phi=0 sign=1
SYMATTR InstName U7
SYMBOL Impedance\\impedance_1phase 160 144 R0
SYMATTR Value2 R=314.159m XL=314.159m
SYMATTR InstName U1
SYMBOL Sources\\v_1phase_3 -64 144 R0
SYMATTR Value U1Nenn={10*hz60}  frequ={fn2} Texp=0m Tpwl=40ms TD=0m fact=0.8165 phi=0
SYMATTR InstName U2
SYMBOL Sources\\v_1phase_3 -16 144 R0
SYMATTR Value U1Nenn={20*Hz100}  frequ={fn3} Texp=0m Tpwl=40ms TD=0m fact=0.8165 phi=0
SYMATTR InstName U3
SYMBOL Meters\\pmeter 80 144 R0
SYMATTR Value sfactor=1  fc=3 fn={fn1}
SYMATTR InstName U4
SYMBOL Meters\\qmeter 112 144 R0
SYMATTR Value sfactor=1  fc=3
SYMATTR InstName U5
TEXT -112 64 Left 2 !.tran 0 550m 0 0.1m
TEXT -112 56 Left 2 !.param tdv=1 tdt=1 fn1=50 fn2=60  fn3=100 hz50=1 hz60=1 hz100=1
TEXT -112 208 Left 5 ;Computation of active power P = Urms*Irms*cos(phi)\nComputation of reactive power Q = Urms*Irms*sin(phi)\nComputation of apparent power S = sqrt(P*P+Q*Q) or Urms*Irms\nNOTE: phi=phiu-phii\n \nHINT: To Get Urms, Irms, phi from FFT-viewer:\n=============================\n1) Simulate the circuit\n2) Click (Activate) the waveformviewerwindow\n3) Choose View/FFT from the menu above\n4) Choose V(in1) by clicking for voltage of circuit one\n5) Choose specify a time range\n6) Choose a timerange wich is the same for all three frequencies (see below)\n7) Choose binomial smoothing 1 point\n8) Right click on left scale\n9) Change db to linear\n10) Write down Urms50,60,100 (57.7V,5.77V,11.6V)\n11) Right click on right scale\n12) Enable this axis \n13) Zoom to 50Hz,60Hz and 100Hz\n14) Write down phase(Urms)=phiu at 50,60,100Hz (+90°,-90°,-90°)\n15) Choose Ix(U4:IN1) by clicking for current \n16) Do the same from 5) to 14) IRMS50,60,10 (130A,15A,16.5A) and phases  phii (-135°,-102°,-146.5°)\n17) Now you can compute Q50(reactive power) in the waveformviewer Urms*Irms*sin(phiu-phii)=5.295kVAr\n18) Now you can compute P50(active power) in the waveformviewer Urms*Irms*cos(phiu-phii)=5.295kW\n19) Now you can compute S50(apparent power) in the waveformviewer Urms*Irms=7.488KVA\n20) Do now the same from 17) to 19) for the 60Hz and the 100Hz voltage and current\n \nChoosing a time range at point 6) which is a multiple at 50,60,100Hz without rest\nfor 50Hz(T=20ms) (50ms-550ms) delta=500ms/20=25x\nfor 60Hz(T=16.667ms) delta=500ms/16.667=30x\nfor 100Hz(T=10ms) delta=500ms=50x
TEXT 40 72 Left 2 ;P50=5.3kW\nQ50=5.3kVAr\nS50=7.5kVA
TEXT 264 24 Left 3 ;Abstract:\nThere is a circuit with three voltage sources\nThe first is a 50Hz voltage source with 100V\nThe second is a 60Hz voltage source with 10V\nThe third is a 100Hz voltage source with 20V\nYou can enable/disable the 50Hz and 60Hz and 100Hz voltage\nby setting hz50=1,0 hz60=1,0 and hz100=1,0\nWe will now compute the active reactive and \napparent power for all three frequencies\nNOTE: The measurement with FFT is better\nthan the measurement mix with pmeter and \nqmeter devices
TEXT -112 960 Left 5 ;Urms50Hz=57.7V  Irms50Hz=130A     phiU=+90°  phiI=45°      Q=5.3kVar  P=5.3kW  S=7.5kVA\nUrms60Hz=5.77V  Irms60Hz=11.76A   phiU=-90°  phiI=-140°  Q=52VAr P=43.6W S=67.8VA\nUrms100Hz=11.54V  Irms100Hz=16.41A  phiU=-90°  phiI=-153.3°  Q=169.2VAr P=85.1W  S=189.4VA
TEXT 96 280 Left 5 ;NOTE: angle = atan(im(X)/re(x))
TEXT -112 1040 Left 5 ;NOTE: at 50Hz Q=P \n      at 60Hz Q>P because XL=2*pi*60Hz rises\n      at 100Hz Q=2*P because XL is now doubled
TEXT 488 1048 Left 2 ;Waveforms: for P,Q,S\n \n57.5*130*sin(90-45)\n57.5*130*cos(90-45)\n57.5*130\n \n5.77*11.76*sin(-90+140)\n5.77*11.76*cos(-90+140)\n5.77*11.76\n \n11.54*16.41*sin(-90+153.3)\n11.54*16.41*cos(-90+153.3)\n11.54*16.41
TEXT -112 128 Left 2 ;100V(50Hz) 10V(60Hz) 20V(100Hz)
TEXT 104 72 Left 2 ;P60=43.6W \nQ60=52VAr\nS60=67.8VA
TEXT 160 72 Left 2 ;P100=85.1W\nQ100=169.2VAr\nS100=189.4VA
